RQ3V1 -- RGB Limited unity-CSC add-on for the BiasiLinux shipping kernel
=========================================================================

Base: the "5.10.89+-7l" tree shipped in the BiasiLinux / PGenerator Pi4
image. Its source tarball lives on every such Pi at
/usr/src/linux-5.10.89+-7l.tar.gz and the kernel build symlink
/lib/modules/5.10.89+-7l/build points at it. This base carries its own
"rgb quant range" connector property (enum: 0 Default, 1 Limited,
2 Full, 3 Reserved, backed by u8 drm_connector_state.rgb_quant_range),
so value 3 is already accepted by stock code -- it just does nothing
useful there.

  Do NOT apply this to a stock raspberrypi/linux tree or to the
  drm_vc4.patch lineage: those bases use broadcast_rgb plumbing and the
  context below does not exist there. Apply it only to the -7l tree.

Effect -- gated entirely on property value 3; values 0/1/2 produce
bit-identical register programming to the unpatched kernel:

  1) vc4_hdmi_is_full_range_rgb(): Reserved(3) reports not-full, so the
     AVI infoframe signals Limited.
  2) vc4_hdmi_csc_setup(): Reserved(3) skips the Full->Limited compress
     matrix; the unconditional trailing HDMI_CSC_CTL write then leaves
     the CSC disabled, i.e. unity passthrough of wire codes.
  3) scripts/mod/modpost.c: vc4's srcversion is prefixed "RQ3V1-" so
     userspace can detect this build via /sys/module/vc4/srcversion.

Why: issue #74. The stock compress path uses a fixed-point gain of
0x1b80/8192 = 0.859375 instead of the exact 219/255 = 0.858824, so the
renderer-expand + kernel-compress round trip drifts some wire codes by
one (~7/220 at 8-bit, far worse modeled at 10-bit). With the CSC in
unity and the renderer drawing wire codes directly there is no
round trip and no drift. Reference design (same value-3 + marker
scheme): BlackJoker90/GPLv3 2e479684.

Companion renderer side: src/ofxRPI4Window/src/ofxRPI4Window.cpp
maps conf RGB Limited (1) onto wire value 3 ONLY when the RQ3V1 marker
is present (rgbLimitedPassthroughSupported()); stock kernels keep the
legacy round-trip. The Pi 5 path never sends 3. The Pi 5-style
vc5_hdmi_csc_setup() variants in vc4_hdmi.c are deliberately not
touched; the Pi 4 uses the vc4 variant.

Build (on the Pi4 itself; the tarball already contains .config,
Module.symvers and prebuilt host scripts, so this is incremental):

  cd /usr/src && tar -xzf linux-5.10.89+-7l.tar.gz
  cd linux-5.10.89+-7l
  patch -p1 --fuzz=0 < /path/to/vc4_rgb_limited_unity.patch
  make prepare && make scripts
  make M=drivers/gpu/drm/vc4 modules

Verify the build carries the marker:

  modinfo -F srcversion drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4.ko    # -> RQ3V1-<hex>

Deploy only after optical acceptance: back up the stock
/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/kernel/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4.ko, replace it,
depmod -a, reboot, and confirm the renderer logs
"PGEN: vc4 RGB Limited passthrough available".

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -136,6 +136,15 @@ static bool vc4_hdmi_is_full_range_rgb(s
 {
 	struct vc4_hdmi_encoder *vc4_encoder = &vc4_hdmi->encoder;
 	
+	/* PGenerator RQ3V1: "rgb quant range" value 3
+	 * (HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_RESERVED) means Limited AVI signalling
+	 * with a unity CSC. Report not-full so the AVI infoframe picks
+	 * LIMITED; vc4_hdmi_csc_setup() leaves the CSC disabled so wire
+	 * codes pass through unchanged. Values 0/1/2 are unaffected.
+	 */
+	if (conn_state->rgb_quant_range == HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_RESERVED)
+		return false;
+
 	if (conn_state->rgb_quant_range == HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_FULL)
 		return true;
 	else
@@ -975,7 +984,8 @@ static void vc4_hdmi_csc_setup(struct vc
 	csc_ctl = VC4_SET_FIELD(VC4_HD_CSC_CTL_ORDER_BGR,
 				VC4_HD_CSC_CTL_ORDER);
 
-	if (!vc4_hdmi_is_full_range_rgb(vc4_hdmi, mode, state)) {
+	if (!vc4_hdmi_is_full_range_rgb(vc4_hdmi, mode, state) &&
+	    state->rgb_quant_range != HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_RESERVED) {
 		/* CEA VICs other than #1 requre limited range RGB
 		 * output unless overridden by an AVI infoframe.
 		 * Apply a colorspace conversion to squash 0-255 down
--- a/scripts/mod/modpost.c
+++ b/scripts/mod/modpost.c
@@ -2072,9 +2072,34 @@ static void read_symbols(const char *mod
 
 	if (!mod->is_vmlinux) {
 		version = get_modinfo(&info, "version");
-		if (version || all_versions)
+		if (version || all_versions) {
 			get_src_version(modname, mod->srcversion,
 					sizeof(mod->srcversion) - 1);
+
+			/* PGenerator RQ3V1: tag vc4's srcversion so the
+			 * renderer detects the RGB Limited unity-CSC build
+			 * via /sys/module/vc4/srcversion. modname is the
+			 * linked .o path here (drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4.o),
+			 * so match that exact suffix. All other modules
+			 * keep the bare md4 digest. The tag truncates
+			 * the digest to fit the prefix, so a tagged
+			 * vc4 srcversion is no longer a pure md4 of
+			 * the module sources.
+			 */
+			if (strlen(modname) >= 17 &&
+			    !strcmp(modname + strlen(modname) - 17,
+				    "gpu/drm/vc4/vc4.o") &&
+			    strlen(mod->srcversion) >= 6) {
+				char tagged[sizeof(mod->srcversion)];
+
+				snprintf(tagged, sizeof(tagged),
+					 "RQ3V1-%.*s",
+					 (int)sizeof(tagged) - 7,
+					 mod->srcversion);
+				memcpy(mod->srcversion, tagged,
+				       sizeof(tagged));
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	parse_elf_finish(&info);
